# No secrets in the repository

**Never** commit credentials to git — including in generated JSON, manifests, logs, or docs.

## Prohibited in tracked files

- GitHub tokens in URLs (`x-access-token:…@github.com`)
- GitHub PATs (`ghp_`, `gho_`, `ghs_`, `github_pat_`)
- Any other API keys, passwords, or private URLs with embedded auth

## Manifest generation

`make generate-books-manifest` derives `owner/repo` from `git remote get-url origin`. In Cloud Agent / CI environments the remote may include an embedded token. The generator **must** strip credentials via `sanitize_github_repo_slug()` in `tools/manifest_books.py`.

When regenerating manifests locally or in automation:

```bash
GITHUB_REPOSITORY=ksteffe/after-certainty make generate-books-manifest \
  MANIFEST_OUT=docs/portfolio-audit/data/books-manifest.json
```

Prefer explicit `GITHUB_REPOSITORY=owner/repo` over relying on authenticated remotes.

## Before commit

1. Run `python3 -m pytest tests/test_no_secrets_in_repo.py -q`
2. If you regenerated `docs/portfolio-audit/data/books-manifest.json` locally (gitignored), spot-check that `repository` is `owner/repo` only (no `https://`, no `@`). Do not commit those snapshots.

CI enforces this via `tests/test_no_secrets_in_repo.py`.
